# JRebirth core

When the repository uses JRebirth, reach for the framework's own patterns before you fall back on plain JavaFX.

Keep the responsibility of every role strictly separated:

- the Application boots the program and configures the shell.
- the Model owns the UI state, the bindings, and the interaction logic.
- the View builds the nodes and delegates the user actions.
- the Controller wires the MVC events together.
- a Command performs one discrete action.
- a Service handles long-running or backend work.
- a Wave carries a message between components.
- a Behavior holds a small piece of shared, cross-cutting logic.

Before you create or refactor any JRebirth code, read the matching skill first.
